I worked right after John.
我在约翰之后紧接着工作。

474
00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:39.590
That's, I think, when we did the clock thing.
我想那应该就是我们拍时钟那场戏的时候。

475
00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:42.230
See, I had no memory of being outside.
你看，我完全不记得自己在外面待过。

476
00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:44.030
I'm outside in that scene.
那场戏里我在外面。

477
00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.310
I'm at the car, and then I'm in the background.
我在车边，然后我在背景里。

478
00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:48.190
We shot all that stuff on the same day.
我们是在同一天拍完所有这些镜头的。

479
00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:50.430
I have no memory of it being cold.
我完全不记得当时很冷。

480
00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.030
Isn't that weird?
这不是很奇怪吗？

481
00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:52.110
You'd think I would remember.
你本以为我会记得的。

482
00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:53.010
You'd think.
你本以为会。

483
00:20:53.130 --> 00:21:00.030
I share on the commentary that I was freezing that morning, that we had had a cold snap, and that was just a real chilly morning.
我在评论音轨里分享过，那天早上我冻坏了，我们当时遇上了一股寒流，那真是一个非常寒冷的早晨。

484
00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:03.750
So, fakie time clock, real breath vapor.
所以，虚假的打卡钟，真实的呼气白雾。

485
00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.070
And real baby belly.
还有真实的孕肚。

486
00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:07.790
My baby belly catch.
我的孕肚特写。

487
00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:13.150
Go to three minutes, 11 seconds, when Pam yells, stop stalling.
跳到3分11秒，当帕姆大喊“别再拖延了”。

488
00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.910
I'll see you, baby bump.
我就能看到你了，小孕肚。

489
00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:23.310
Well, this is the episode where I described in our book that I had gone to J.Crew over the weekend and bought myself a new outfit,
嗯，这一集就是我在书里描述过的那一集，我周末去了J.Crew给自己买了一套新衣服，

490
00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.610
because I realized I was not going to make it to the end of the season.
因为我意识到我撑不到这一季结束了。

491
00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:29.770
You were busting out of your button-down Pam shirt.
你当时快把帕姆那件扣子衬衫给撑破了。

492
00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:30.490
So much.
确实如此。

493
00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.990
And you tried to hide it.
而且你还试图遮掩。

494
00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:32.510
I did.
我确实试过。

495
00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:38.790
That's my little boy in there.
那是我的小男孩在里面。

496
00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:39.210
I know.
我知道。

497
00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:42.970
Well, now we're going to see the bullpen under Dwight's supervision.
好了，现在我们要看看在德怀特监管下的办公区了。

498
00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:46.070
I went to the shooting draft to see how it was described.
我查阅了拍摄剧本，看看它是怎么描述的。

499
00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:46.670
Okay.
好的。

500
00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:48.570
Interior office reception.
内景，办公室接待处。

501
00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.450
People are walking in for the day.
大家正陆续走进办公室开始新的一天。

502
00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:55.970
Stanley punches in and walks past an American flag and a framed portrait of Dwight.
斯坦利打卡上班，走过一面美国国旗和一幅德怀特的装裱肖像画。

503
00:21:55.970 --> 00:22:02.310
Andy at his desk takes off his windbreaker, revealing he is wearing a short-sleeved shirt like the one Dwight wears.
安迪在办公桌前脱下防风外套，露出里面穿着的短袖衬衫，和德怀特平时穿的一模一样。

504
00:22:02.690 --> 00:22:06.630
We hear the beep of a watch alarm coming from what is now Dwight's office.
我们听到从现在的德怀特办公室里传出手表闹钟的滴滴声。

505
00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:08.590
Dwight walks out with a smile.
德怀特微笑着走了出来。

506
00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:13.090
He kicks the front door shut and says, let's begin.
他踢上大门，说道，我们开始吧。

507
00:22:13.090 --> 00:22:16.750
So I noticed a couple of things in this scene.
我注意到了这个场景里的几件事。

508
00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:24.430
First of all, at four minutes, when Dwight walks up to start to lead everyone in the Pledge of Allegiance,
首先，在四分钟的时候，当德怀特走上前准备带领大家宣誓效忠时，

509
00:22:24.590 --> 00:22:30.510
followed by his morning announcements, there's a shot of the messages container.
紧接着是他的晨间公告，镜头扫过了留言盒。

510
00:22:30.790 --> 00:22:32.190
You know, the thing on reception?
你知道的，就是前台那个东西？

511
00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:35.210
D'Angelo Vickers is still getting messages.
迪安杰洛·维克斯还在接收留言。

512
00:22:35.630 --> 00:22:38.450
His name is still on the little message thing.
他的名字还在那个小留言板上。

513
00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:41.530
We also got a fan question from Stephen M.
我们还收到了一位来自旧金山的粉丝斯蒂芬·M的提问，

514
00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:43.290
in San Francisco who said,
他问道，

515
00:22:43.450 --> 00:22:46.690
I noticed that Andy was wearing a short-sleeved business suit.
我注意到安迪穿了一件短袖商务衬衫。

516
00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:54.330
Was this a nod to his usual sucking up to the manager by replicating Dwight's style choices?
这是不是在暗示他通过模仿德怀特的穿衣风格来讨好经理？

517
00:22:54.810 --> 00:22:55.470
Yes.
是的。

518
00:22:55.630 --> 00:23:01.950
So we shot that little moment of him taking off his windbreaker and then Dwight clocks it.
所以我们拍了他脱掉防风外套的那个小片段，然后德怀特注意到了。

519
00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:06.750
And when they did their writer's screening, because they would do that,
当他们进行编剧内部试映时，因为他们确实会这样做，

520
00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:09.470
they would screen the episodes for the writers while they were editing.
他们会在剪辑时为编剧们放映剧集。

521
00:23:09.670 --> 00:23:14.770
He said it got a huge laugh in the room, but ultimately it had to get cut for time.
他说那个片段在现场引起了哄堂大笑，但最终因为时长原因被剪掉了。

522
00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:18.370
So then you just see Andy wearing the short-sleeved shirt and it's not really explained.
所以你最后只看到安迪穿着那件短袖衬衫，并没有得到真正的解释。

523
00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:21.370
It's now time for everyone to say the Pledge of Allegiance.
现在是大家宣誓效忠的时间了。

524
00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:26.810
Behind Dwight is a huge painting of himself looking like a dictator.
德怀特身后是一幅巨大的画像，画里的他看起来像个独裁者。

525
00:23:27.430 --> 00:23:29.350
Angela's very into this Pledge of Allegiance.
安吉拉非常投入这次宣誓效忠。

526
00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:31.330
She's kind of into this whole mood, I think.
我觉得她挺享受这种氛围的。

527
00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:32.910
I think she is too.
我也觉得是。

528
00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:36.930
We got a bunch of fan mail about you, Angela, in this Pledge of Allegiance.
我们收到了很多关于你在这次宣誓效忠中表现的粉丝来信，安吉拉。

529
00:23:37.050 --> 00:23:40.870
People want to know if your amen was scripted or improvised.
大家想知道你的那句“阿门”是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的。

530
00:23:41.490 --> 00:23:43.050
Y'all, I improvised that.
各位，那是我即兴发挥的。

531
00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:46.690
I was so delighted it made it in.
我很高兴它被保留在了正片里。

532
00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:49.530
We also got a fan question from David P.
我们还收到了一位来自宾夕法尼亚州的粉丝大卫·P的提问，

533
00:23:49.590 --> 00:23:50.130
in Pennsylvania,
他注意到奥斯卡没有说，

534
00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:53.290
who noticed that Oscar does not say,
“上帝保佑的国家”。

535
00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:55.570
One Nation Under God.
而且他还对着镜头看了一眼。

536
00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:57.590
And he even gives a look to camera.
想知道那是不是剧本安排的。

537
00:23:57.930 --> 00:23:59.770
Wanted to know if that was scripted.
那是剧本写的。

538
00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:01.650
That was scripted.
贾斯汀说他听说有些人认为这暗示了奥斯卡是个无神论者，

539
00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:06.170
Justin said he heard that some people thought that this implied that Oscar is an atheist,
但这并非贾斯汀的本意。

540
00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:08.550
but that was not Justin's intention.
他说他只是觉得奥斯卡是那种会反感在工作场所被强迫谈论上帝的人，

541
00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:14.830
He said he just figured that Oscar was the kind of guy who would resent being made to talk about God
他会非常自豪且非常自鸣得意地公开拒绝配合。

542
00:24:14.830 --> 00:24:20.230
in the workplace, and he would very proudly and very smugly publicly abstain.
所以他才写了那一段。

543
00:24:20.830 --> 00:24:22.590
And so that's why he wrote that bit.
我敢打赌奥斯卡早就准备好这一出了。

544
00:24:22.710 --> 00:24:25.710
I bet Oscar has that actually ready to go.
没错。

545
00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:26.470
Exactly.
在晨间公告里，德怀特要通知大家复印机代码的事，还有，

546
00:24:26.470 --> 00:24:31.970
In the morning announcements, Dwight is going to let everyone know about the copier codes and also
乔·贝内特要来参加他和盖博之间的高层会议。

547
00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:36.810
that Joe Bennett is coming for a high-level meeting between him and Gabe.
所谓的“高层”，其实就是一次普通的会面和寒暄。

548
00:24:37.130 --> 00:24:39.430
And by high-level, it's just a general meet and greet.
嗯哼。

549
00:24:39.630 --> 00:24:39.990
Mm-hmm.
凯莉会迟到。

550
00:24:40.490 --> 00:24:42.290
Kelly is going to be late.
凯莉会迟到。

551
00:24:42.470 --> 00:24:45.470
She comes in like a back door.
她像走后门一样溜了进来。

552
00:24:45.910 --> 00:24:46.350
Sneaky.
真鬼祟。

553
00:24:46.550 --> 00:24:47.670
How often is she late?
她迟到的频率高吗？

554
00:24:47.670 --> 00:24:50.770
If she always comes in that back door, you know Michael wasn't looking for her.
如果她总是走那个后门，你就知道迈克尔没在留意她。

555
00:24:50.930 --> 00:24:52.610
I don't think we've ever used that door.
我觉得我们从来没用过那扇门。

556
00:24:52.610 --> 00:24:58.050
Well, she said she had an illness of a personal nature, and Dwight wants to know which part of her body.
嗯，她说她得了某种私人疾病，德怀特想知道是身体的哪个部位。

557
00:24:58.390 --> 00:25:00.010
Mindy could not keep this together.
敏迪根本憋不住笑。

558
00:25:00.230 --> 00:25:00.470
No.
没错。

559
00:25:00.530 --> 00:25:02.350
She was laughing so hard every single time.
她每次都笑得特别厉害。

560
00:25:02.350 --> 00:25:03.450
As he was like pointing?
是因为他当时在指指点点吗？

561
00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:04.170
Yes.
是的。

562
00:25:04.930 --> 00:25:07.790
And I'm surprised they even got a take without her laughing.
我很惊讶他们竟然能拍出一条她没笑场的镜头。

563
00:25:08.330 --> 00:25:14.850
Now we're going to start this Gabe-Andy runner, where Gabe is just trying so desperately to win Aaron back,
现在我们要开始讲盖博和安迪的这段剧情了，盖博拼命想把艾琳追回来，

564
00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:16.950
and he doesn't want Andy flirting with her.
他不想让安迪跟她调情。

565
00:25:17.490 --> 00:25:21.810
No, he grabs Andy and brings him into the conference room, and they close all the blinds.
没错，他把安迪拉进会议室，然后关上了所有的百叶窗。

566
00:25:22.390 --> 00:25:25.230
I loved this spy shot through the blinds.
我超爱这个透过百叶窗拍的间谍视角镜头。

567
00:25:25.330 --> 00:25:27.470
There is only a two-inch space.
只有两英寸的缝隙。

568
00:25:27.470 --> 00:25:30.430
You see the whole scene play out in two inches.
你能在两英寸的视野里看到整场戏的展开。

569
00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:36.210
Basically, he makes Andy promise to never date Aaron again, makes him say it.
基本上，他逼安迪发誓永远不再和艾琳约会，还让他亲口说出来。

570
00:25:36.310 --> 00:25:40.110
And he's so overbearing that Andy kind of agrees.
他太咄咄逼人了，安迪只能勉强答应。

571
00:25:40.350 --> 00:25:41.510
He just wants out of there.
他只想赶紧离开那儿。

572
00:25:41.610 --> 00:25:43.410
Andy's like, get me out of this conference room.
安迪当时的心情就是：快让我离开这间会议室。

573
00:25:43.410 --> 00:25:47.450
In the meantime, Jim has started his sabotaging of Dwight.
与此同时，吉姆开始了他对德怀特的恶作剧。

574
00:25:48.410 --> 00:25:54.390
You know, there are a bunch of deleted scenes on the DVD where he gets Jordan to prank Dwight with him.
你知道，DVD里有很多删减片段，里面他拉着乔丹一起捉弄德怀特。

575
00:25:54.570 --> 00:25:56.490
And Jenna, it did not sit well with me.
珍娜，这让我感觉很不舒服。

576
00:25:56.630 --> 00:25:57.030
No.
确实。

577
00:25:57.030 --> 00:26:00.630
I was like, why is Jordan pranking Dwight with you and not Pam?
我当时就在想，为什么是乔丹跟你一起捉弄德怀特，而不是帕姆？

578
00:26:00.630 --> 00:26:03.130
I didn't like it, and I'm glad they were deleted.
我不喜欢那样，很高兴那些片段被删了。

579
00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:07.890
Well, I remember seeing an early cut of this episode, and there was a talking head with Jordan.
我记得看过这集的一个早期剪辑版，里面有一个乔丹的采访镜头。

580
00:26:07.890 --> 00:26:18.910
Where she says something to the effect of like, well, there's one person in the office I don't mind, or something like that, meaning Jim after this day of pranking.
她说了一些类似“办公室里有一个人我不讨厌”之类的话，指的就是经历这一天的恶作剧后的吉姆。

581
00:26:19.050 --> 00:26:25.810
It's on the DVDs, and she smiles and lights up and looks so beautiful, and she's so, like, tickled by Jim.
那段在DVD里，她笑得很灿烂，看起来特别美，而且她被吉姆逗得很开心。

582
00:26:25.930 --> 00:26:28.390
And I was like, uh-uh, that would have made people lose their minds.
我当时就想，不行，那会让观众抓狂的。

583
00:26:28.630 --> 00:26:30.550
Yeah, that all went goodbye.
是啊，那些全都被删掉了。

584
00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:35.030
Well, Jim is going to try to start a social club called The FiSt.
吉姆打算成立一个叫“拳头”的社交俱乐部。

585
00:26:35.710 --> 00:26:37.770
Dwight sees this, of course, as a rebellion.
德怀特当然把这看作是一种反叛。

586
00:26:38.410 --> 00:26:44.650
Jim says, listen, I'd love to have you come in today, but it's just that today we're really busy with Operation Overthrow.
吉姆说，听着，我很想让你今天加入，但我们今天忙着执行“推翻行动”。

587
00:26:45.590 --> 00:26:46.990
It's not a big deal, but.
没什么大不了的，但是。

588
00:26:47.150 --> 00:26:48.450
What was Jim's morning like?
吉姆那天早上在干什么？

589
00:26:48.570 --> 00:26:53.650
He wouldn't come inside, then he did come inside, then he made a whole bunch of flyers, used a lot of black ink.
他一开始不肯进来，后来又进来了，然后印了一大堆传单，用了好多黑色墨水。

590
00:26:53.790 --> 00:26:54.230
He did.
确实。

591
00:26:54.590 --> 00:26:56.250
He's been very busy at the copier.
他在复印机前忙得不可开交。

592
00:26:56.970 --> 00:26:57.370
Oh.
噢。

593
00:26:57.710 --> 00:26:59.310
Why wasn't he at the copier?
为什么他没在复印机那儿？

594
00:26:59.310 --> 00:26:59.930
I don't know.
我不知道。

595
00:27:00.550 --> 00:27:06.890
Well, Angela is stuck behind Kevin at the copier as he tries to type in his 21-digit copy code.
安吉拉被凯文堵在复印机后面，因为他正试图输入他那21位数的复印代码。

596
00:27:07.350 --> 00:27:10.650
This was one of my favorite scenes to do in all of Season 7.
这是我在第七季里最喜欢演的场景之一。

597
00:27:11.030 --> 00:27:13.930
I loved doing this bit with Craig and Brian.
我很喜欢和克雷格还有布莱恩一起演这段戏。

598
00:27:14.050 --> 00:27:20.270
We were having the absolute time of our lives, and it's going to come back later, and I'll share more then.
我们当时玩得简直太开心了，这段剧情后面还会再出现，到时候我再分享更多细节。

599
00:27:20.610 --> 00:27:23.390
Well, I have a fan catch from Shanley S.
好的，我收到一条来自阿拉斯加州安克雷奇的珊莉·S发来的粉丝发现。

600
00:27:23.590 --> 00:27:24.650
in Anchorage, Alaska.
在阿拉斯加州的安克雷奇。

601
00:27:25.270 --> 00:27:30.250
At 6 minutes and 40 seconds, you can see a solitaire game on the computer screen behind Kevin
在6分40秒的时候，你可以看到凯文身后的电脑屏幕上在玩纸牌游戏

602
00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:31.530
when he's at the copier.
当时他正在复印机旁。

603
00:27:31.930 --> 00:27:34.230
So not everyone was worried about the copier.
所以并不是每个人都在担心复印机的事。

604
00:27:34.370 --> 00:27:35.590
Some people were playing solitaire.
有些人还在玩纸牌。

605
00:27:35.590 --> 00:27:40.690
Well, Andy is now going to try to show Pam a video, and it's blocked.
安迪现在打算给帕姆看个视频，结果被屏蔽了。

606
00:27:40.970 --> 00:27:41.930
The website is blocked.
网站被屏蔽了。

607
00:27:42.070 --> 00:27:42.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

608
00:27:42.750 --> 00:27:43.870
Internet blocked.
互联网被封了。

609
00:27:44.270 --> 00:27:50.970
This was a bigger runner, and it was driving everyone crazy because Dwight limited their internet access.
这是一个很长的梗，让大家都快疯了，因为德怀特限制了他们的网络访问权限。

610
00:27:51.550 --> 00:27:53.410
Phyllis was really struggling with it.
菲利斯为此真的很苦恼。

611
00:27:53.490 --> 00:27:54.970
