不想让吉姆，你知道的，惹出什么麻烦。

773
00:34:34.040 --> 00:34:34.480
That's right.
没错。

774
00:34:34.660 --> 00:34:36.140
No pranking with Joe here.
乔在这里的时候不能搞恶作剧。

775
00:34:36.860 --> 00:34:38.480
Jim really takes in the room.
吉姆仔细打量着房间。

776
00:34:38.620 --> 00:34:41.640
He's like, wow, you know, this is quite the decor.
他就像是在说，哇，你知道，这装饰真够特别的。

777
00:34:42.260 --> 00:34:44.840
And Dwight starts to point things out to him.
然后德怀特开始向他指出一些东西。

778
00:34:45.540 --> 00:34:50.100
Yes, this is when we learn that the gun on his desk is a Beaumont AdaMs.
是的，这时我们才知道他桌上的枪是博蒙特·亚当斯手枪。

779
00:34:50.440 --> 00:34:54.200
Yeah, he thought maybe, you know, Joe might like it, might give them something to talk about.
是的，他觉得也许，你知道，乔可能会喜欢它，可能会给他们提供一些谈资。

780
00:34:54.440 --> 00:34:55.920
Yeah, I guess she collects guns.
是的，我猜她收集枪支。

781
00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:56.320
Yeah.
是的。

782
00:34:56.320 --> 00:34:56.840
Okay.
好的。

783
00:34:57.320 --> 00:35:04.460
Also, this is when he mentions his rescue piranha as well as his desk, which is, he says,
另外，这时他还提到了他的救援食人鱼以及他的办公桌，他说，

784
00:35:04.560 --> 00:35:07.260
a replica of Uday Hussein's desk.
那是乌代·侯赛因办公桌的复制品。

785
00:35:07.400 --> 00:35:09.020
He read an article in Newsweek.
他读过《新闻周刊》上的一篇文章。

786
00:35:09.540 --> 00:35:12.160
Here's something I remember about that desk, Angela.
关于那张桌子，我记得一件事，安吉拉。

787
00:35:12.420 --> 00:35:15.160
I remember that it was made out of wood.
我记得它是木头做的。

788
00:35:15.320 --> 00:35:19.140
It was very light and they painted it to look like marble.
它非常轻，他们把它漆成了大理石的样子。

789
00:35:19.340 --> 00:35:24.700
And I would just go in and stare at it because I was so impressed with this painting job.
我经常走进去盯着它看，因为我对这种漆工印象太深刻了。

790
00:35:24.880 --> 00:35:25.740
I thought it was amazing.
我觉得它太棒了。

791
00:35:26.320 --> 00:35:31.280
You know what I thought about when I rewatched this episode was if that desk was truly marble
你知道我在重温这一集时想到的是什么吗，如果那张桌子真的是大理石做的

792
00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:34.900
and that big, they would not have been able to get it through the door and in the room.
而且那么大，他们根本没法把它搬进门并放进房间里。

793
00:35:35.120 --> 00:35:38.180
You would have to build a room around that desk.
你得围着那张桌子建一个房间才行。

794
00:35:38.620 --> 00:35:44.240
Also, in the commentary, Justin and Mindy shared that it was Mindy's idea to have this desk.
另外，在评论音轨里，贾斯汀和敏迪分享说，拥有这张桌子是敏迪的主意。

795
00:35:44.240 --> 00:35:45.880
Oh, I love it.
噢，我喜欢这个点子。

796
00:35:45.980 --> 00:35:48.680
Well, this was a whole thing, this desk, how they built it.
嗯，这整件事，这张桌子，他们是怎么把它造出来的。

797
00:35:48.780 --> 00:35:52.180
I asked Randy because I told him my memory of loving it.
我问了兰迪，因为我告诉他我记得我很喜欢它。

798
00:35:52.420 --> 00:35:59.120
And he said the writers had originally pitched that the desk was like a solid black onyx.
他说编剧们最初提议这张桌子应该是纯黑玛瑙做的。

799
00:35:59.960 --> 00:36:05.740
But Michael Gallenberg, our production designer, said that that would just suck out all the light in the room.
但我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格说，那样会吸走房间里所有的光线。

800
00:36:05.840 --> 00:36:07.260
It wouldn't look good on camera.
在镜头前看起来效果不会好。

801
00:36:07.460 --> 00:36:11.060
And he thought it would be more visually interesting if we made it out of marble.
他觉得如果我们用大理石做的话，视觉效果会更有趣。

802
00:36:11.060 --> 00:36:14.520
So Tim James built it out of lumber.
所以蒂姆·詹姆斯用木材把它做了出来。

803
00:36:14.760 --> 00:36:23.820
And then we hired this guy, Ron Henson, who is an amazing painter, to paint it to look like marble.
然后我们雇了罗恩·亨森，一位了不起的画家，让他把它画得看起来像大理石一样。

804
00:36:24.380 --> 00:36:28.160
Well, you would never know that that was like a fakie desk.
嗯，你绝对看不出那是个假桌子。

805
00:36:28.340 --> 00:36:29.280
It looks so good.
看起来太棒了。

806
00:36:29.900 --> 00:36:34.520
Justin said there was a reason why they over-decorated Dwight's office.
贾斯汀说他们过度装饰德怀特办公室是有原因的。

807
00:36:35.340 --> 00:36:39.600
And it was because they wanted to, quote, unquote, hide the gun.
原因就是他们想，引用一下，隐藏那把枪。

808
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:41.840
He said that audiences are really smart.
他说观众真的很聪明。

809
00:36:42.140 --> 00:36:46.880
That audiences know if you introduce a gun into a storyline, that gun is going to go off.
观众知道如果你在剧情中引入一把枪，那把枪迟早会走火。

810
00:36:47.160 --> 00:36:49.340
I guess it's called Chekhov's gun.
我想这叫契诃夫之枪。

811
00:36:49.600 --> 00:36:51.460
It's like a writer's theory.
这就像一种编剧理论。

812
00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:51.960
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

813
00:36:51.960 --> 00:37:02.440
Okay, so he thought that if he did everything he could to make the gun feel just like a minor prop, among other ridiculous props, maybe, just maybe,
好吧，他认为如果他尽其所能让这把枪看起来只是个不起眼的道具，混在一堆荒唐的道具里，也许，仅仅是也许，

814
00:37:02.660 --> 00:37:06.060
the fact that Dwight fires the gun later would be a surprise.
德怀特后来开枪这件事会成为一个惊喜。

815
00:37:06.320 --> 00:37:09.580
Well, I think he did a good job because he put it in a glass box.
嗯，我觉得他做得很好，因为他把它放在了一个玻璃盒子里。

816
00:37:09.840 --> 00:37:11.660
I didn't think it was going to get used.
我当时以为它不会被用到。

817
00:37:11.660 --> 00:37:15.640
I thought it was just another one of Dwight's swords and daggers and armor.
我以为那只是德怀特的又一把剑、匕首或盔甲之类的东西。

818
00:37:15.980 --> 00:37:16.240
Yeah.
是啊。

819
00:37:16.660 --> 00:37:20.840
Justin said on the commentary, Jenna, that they broke down this episode so many times.
贾斯汀在评论音轨里说，珍娜，他们把这一集拆解分析了很多次。

820
00:37:20.840 --> 00:37:28.460
It was a bit of a puzzle trying to figure out how to make Dwight the manager and what that would look like, but then also where would it go?
要搞清楚如何让德怀特当上经理，那会是什么样子，以及之后剧情该怎么发展，这确实像个难题，但后来，

821
00:37:28.920 --> 00:37:35.160
And it was the writer Steve Healy's idea that Dwight would become manager and screw it up all in one week.
编剧史蒂夫·希利提议让德怀特当上经理，然后在一周内把事情搞砸。

822
00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:36.380
Oh, that's fun.
哦，那很有意思。

823
00:37:36.520 --> 00:37:43.160
So you had to have a big thing that would, like, sabotage him being manager because he was probably going to be pretty good at it.
所以你得安排一件大事，比如破坏他当经理的进程，因为他本来可能会干得相当不错。

824
00:37:43.280 --> 00:37:43.560
Right.
没错。

825
00:37:44.080 --> 00:37:46.680
Well, in the next scene, Dwight's going to open up a package.
嗯，在下一场戏里，德怀特要拆开一个包裹。

826
00:37:47.860 --> 00:37:50.800
And inside is a gun holster.
里面是一个枪套。

827
00:37:51.100 --> 00:37:52.520
From his Uncle Honk.
是他洪克叔叔送的。

828
00:37:52.800 --> 00:37:53.280
Yes.
是的。

829
00:37:53.740 --> 00:37:55.420
And he's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

830
00:37:55.500 --> 00:37:56.360
He's so touched.
他非常感动。

831
00:37:56.560 --> 00:37:56.740
Yeah.
是啊。

832
00:37:57.180 --> 00:37:59.620
Well, Dwight immediately takes his gun holster.
嗯，德怀特立刻拿起了他的枪套。

833
00:37:59.860 --> 00:38:00.960
He puts his gun in it.
他把枪放了进去。

834
00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:03.020
And he starts parading around the office.
然后开始在办公室里招摇过市。

835
00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:03.560
Yeah.
是啊。

836
00:38:04.120 --> 00:38:06.360
Everyone's like, Dwight, what are you doing?
大家都说，德怀特，你在干什么？

837
00:38:06.360 --> 00:38:08.840
You can't just walk around with a gun in the office.
你不能就这样在办公室里带着枪走来走去。

838
00:38:09.260 --> 00:38:12.140
And he's like, but my Uncle Honk made this for me.
他说，可是这是我洪克叔叔为我做的。

839
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:13.480
This is so special.
这太特别了。

840
00:38:13.480 --> 00:38:17.740
Yeah, he's like, you can't, like, just walk around without a gun in it.
是啊，他说，你不能，就是，不能不放枪在里面就走来走去。

841
00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:19.640
You have to put the gun in it.
你必须把枪放进去。

842
00:38:19.740 --> 00:38:21.240
And everyone's, like, pitching ideas.
大家都在出主意。

843
00:38:21.240 --> 00:38:22.760
Well, why don't you put your phone in it?
嗯，你为什么不把手机放进去呢？

844
00:38:22.840 --> 00:38:24.300
Why don't you put a banana in it?
你为什么不放根香蕉进去呢？

845
00:38:24.580 --> 00:38:27.840
I would have loved to seen him walking around with a banana in that holster.
我真想看他腰间挂着那个枪套，里面插着根香蕉走来走去。

846
00:38:28.020 --> 00:38:31.260
I thought it was a good suggestion, actually, I have to say.
说实话，我觉得那是个好建议。

847
00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:33.780
Pam is going to threaten to call Joe.
帕姆威胁说要给乔打电话。

848
00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:37.520
And that's when Dwight is like, fine.
就在那时，德怀特说，好吧。

849
00:38:38.280 --> 00:38:40.720
And he does a little twirly thing with the gun.
他拿着枪做了一个小小的旋转动作。

850
00:38:40.720 --> 00:38:45.180
He's going to put it back in the holster, but instead it fires right into the ground,
他本想把它放回枪套里，结果枪却直接走火射向了地面，

851
00:38:45.460 --> 00:38:46.860
right next to Andy's ear.
就在安迪的耳朵旁边。

852
00:38:47.580 --> 00:38:49.300
And Andy grabs his ear.
然后安迪抓住了他的耳朵。

853
00:38:49.660 --> 00:38:53.940
On the commentary, they were like, this was a really strong cutaway because that was the
在评论音轨里，他们说这是一个非常强有力的转场，因为那是

854
00:38:53.940 --> 00:38:54.460
act break.
幕间休息。

855
00:38:55.160 --> 00:38:56.900
That's a pretty strong act break.
那是一个相当强有力的幕间休息。

856
00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:59.940
Well, we got a lot of questions about this moment.
嗯，我们收到了很多关于这个时刻的问题。

857
00:39:00.260 --> 00:39:03.200
First of all, Dash P from Connecticut said,
首先，来自康涅狄格州的Dash P问道：

858
00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:08.680
Did Rain fire a blank or was the flash and gunshot sound added in post?
Rain开的是空包弹，还是枪火和枪声是后期加进去的？

859
00:39:09.100 --> 00:39:11.060
No, that was not added in poSt.
不，那不是后期加进去的。

860
00:39:11.260 --> 00:39:12.360
Rain fired a blank.
Rain开的是空包弹。

861
00:39:12.540 --> 00:39:14.180
That was a real working gun.
那是一把真正能用的枪。

862
00:39:14.680 --> 00:39:20.140
Randy explained that a blank is a cartridge that contains no projectile.
兰迪解释说，空包弹是一种不含弹头的弹药。

863
00:39:20.260 --> 00:39:22.100
It just has gunpowder in it.
里面只有火药。

864
00:39:22.700 --> 00:39:28.900
We used what was called a quarter round, which holds about a fourth of the amount of gunpowder,
我们用的是所谓的四分之一装药，大概只装了四分之一的火药量，

865
00:39:29.040 --> 00:39:29.560
I guess.
我想是这样。

866
00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:32.700
But still, firing a blank can be really dangerous.
但即便如此，发射空包弹仍然非常危险。

867
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:36.220
And even a quarter round makes a very loud noise.
而且即使是四分之一装药也会产生巨大的噪音。

868
00:39:36.220 --> 00:39:38.440
It produces that muzzle flash.
它会产生那种枪口火光。

869
00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:44.360
So in order to do this, the crew held multiple rehearsals without any cast on set.
所以为了拍摄这一幕，剧组在没有演员在场的情况下进行了多次排练。

870
00:39:44.760 --> 00:39:46.440
We had a full safety meeting.
我们开了个完整的安全会议。

871
00:39:46.440 --> 00:39:47.480
I remember that.
我记得那个。

872
00:39:47.720 --> 00:39:52.040
And they handed out those special shooter's earplugs for us all to wear.
他们分发了那种特制的射击耳塞让我们大家都戴上。

873
00:39:52.220 --> 00:39:52.700
Just for the sound.
只是为了隔音。

874
00:39:52.700 --> 00:39:54.100
Because it was a very loud noise.
因为那声音非常大。

875
00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:55.160
It's a very loud pop.
那是一声非常响的爆鸣。

876
00:39:55.500 --> 00:39:57.500
And Randy said we did it in one take.
兰迪说我们一次就拍过了。

877
00:39:58.360 --> 00:40:02.940
Well, one of the things they talked about on the commentary was the idea that Dwight does
嗯，他们在评论音轨中谈论的一件事是，德怀特做的事情

878
00:40:02.940 --> 00:40:08.420
something that's definitely going to get him removed from acting manager, but also making
肯定会让他被撤掉代理经理的职务，但同时也确保

879
00:40:08.420 --> 00:40:12.160
sure the way they shot it, it was very clear that no one was injured.
拍摄方式非常明确地显示没有人受伤。

880
00:40:12.980 --> 00:40:17.620
We also got a fan question from Zach T in Illinois, who said,
我们还收到了来自伊利诺伊州Zach T的粉丝提问，他说：

881
00:40:18.040 --> 00:40:24.860
regarding Dwight's gun, after doing some research, it seems that the gun that Dwight used resembles a
关于德怀特的枪，经过一番研究，德怀特使用的枪似乎类似于

882
00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:28.660
Remington 1875 American-made revolver.
雷明顿1875美制左轮手枪。

883
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:35.080
However, Dwight refers to it as a Beaumont Adams, which was a British service revolver from the
然而，德怀特称它为博蒙特-亚当斯左轮手枪，那是一种英国制式左轮手枪，

884
00:40:35.080 --> 00:40:36.480
mid-late 19th century.
源自19世纪中后期。

885
00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:41.020
That actually looks very different than the gun that was used in this episode.
那看起来实际上和这一集中使用的枪非常不同。

886
00:40:41.460 --> 00:40:47.020
What gun was used for the prop, and how did the writers decide on calling it a Beaumont
这集道具用的是什么枪？编剧们为什么决定把它叫作博蒙特-亚当斯，

887
00:40:47.020 --> 00:40:51.140
Adams, despite the fact that it looks nothing like a Beaumont Adams?
尽管它看起来一点也不像博蒙特-亚当斯？

888
00:40:52.200 --> 00:40:53.880
Well, Zach, good catch.
嗯，Zach，观察得很仔细。

889
00:40:54.100 --> 00:40:55.840
That was not a Beaumont AdaMs.
那确实不是博蒙特-亚当斯。

890
00:40:56.140 --> 00:41:03.320
So we hired an armorer for this scene, and he informed us that there are no credible working
我们为这场戏聘请了一位军械师，他告诉我们，市面上没有可靠的、可运作的

891
00:41:03.320 --> 00:41:05.260
replicas of a Beaumont AdaMs.
博蒙特-亚当斯复刻版。

892
00:41:05.260 --> 00:41:06.760
It, like, couldn't be found.
它根本找不到。

893
00:41:06.940 --> 00:41:10.980
He said, we could have one built, but it would take months.
他说，我们可以定制一把，但这需要几个月的时间。

894
00:41:11.180 --> 00:41:11.800
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

895
00:41:12.020 --> 00:41:17.680
So the producers decided to go with this Remington 1875.
所以制片人决定使用这把雷明顿1875。

896
00:41:18.200 --> 00:41:24.360
It was a modern-day build of a classic revolver, and because this was not some sort of antique
它是经典左轮手枪的现代复刻版，而且因为它不是那种古董

897
00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:28.880
gun, but a modern-made gun, it was considered safer to handle.
枪支，而是现代制造的枪，所以被认为操作起来更安全。

898
00:41:29.080 --> 00:41:30.560
It could really fire a blank.
它确实可以发射空包弹。

899
00:41:31.020 --> 00:41:32.760
So we went with that.
所以我们就选了那把。

900
00:41:32.760 --> 00:41:36.980
But the writers chose to keep the Beaumont Adams reference just because they thought it
但编剧们选择保留博蒙特-亚当斯的称呼，只是因为他们觉得它

901
00:41:36.980 --> 00:41:41.300
was funny, and that it sounded like something that Joe might recognize and appreciate.
这很有趣，而且听起来像是乔可能会认出来并欣赏的东西。

902
00:41:42.220 --> 00:41:47.000
Justin said, internet gun aficionados have called them out on this cheat before.
贾斯汀说，互联网上的枪械爱好者以前就曾指出过这种作弊行为。

903
00:41:47.540 --> 00:41:50.300
You know, Angela, I remember it was loud.
安吉拉，你知道吗，我记得当时声音很大。

904
00:41:50.560 --> 00:41:51.220
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

905
00:41:51.480 --> 00:41:51.660
Yeah.
记得。

906
00:41:51.660 --> 00:41:53.820
I mean, we didn't have to pretend to jump.
我的意思是，我们不需要假装跳起来。

907
00:41:54.020 --> 00:41:56.120
No, all of our reactions were very real.
没错，我们所有的反应都是非常真实的。

908
00:41:56.240 --> 00:41:56.940
For sure.
确实。

909
00:41:57.960 --> 00:42:04.360
At 11 minutes and 26 seconds, Oscar is going to examine the gunshot hole that is in the floor.
在11分26秒时，奥斯卡会去检查地板上的那个弹孔。

910
00:42:04.620 --> 00:42:05.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

911
00:42:05.320 --> 00:42:05.640
Right?
对吧？

912
00:42:05.920 --> 00:42:06.220
Yes.
是的。

913
00:42:06.220 --> 00:42:09.920
And he's going to say, look at that, hardwood floors underneath this carpet.
然后他会说，看那儿，地毯下面是硬木地板。

914
00:42:10.120 --> 00:42:10.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

915
00:42:10.780 --> 00:42:11.460
All along.
一直都是。

916
00:42:11.720 --> 00:42:17.160
I would like to point out that while Oscar is examining the damage to the floors, you can
我想指出的是，当奥斯卡在检查地板损坏情况时，你可以

917
00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:19.740
see that John had a heater under his desk.
看到约翰的桌子底下有个取暖器。

918
00:42:20.160 --> 00:42:20.640
What?
什么？

919
00:42:21.060 --> 00:42:21.460
Yeah.
是的。

920
00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:22.460
John?
约翰？

921
00:42:22.720 --> 00:42:26.860
All this time, I thought it was just us, but John has a heater under his desk.
一直以来，我还以为只有我们这样，结果约翰的桌子底下也有个取暖器。

922
00:42:27.020 --> 00:42:27.740
I took a picture.
我拍了张照片。

923
00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:31.360
I am like, I'm shocked right now.
我当时就想，我现在太震惊了。

924
00:42:31.360 --> 00:42:32.960
I was shocked as well.
我也很震惊。

925
00:42:33.180 --> 00:42:37.240
I know I should be, like, focusing on the episode and this big plot point just happened,
我知道我应该专注于这一集，而且刚刚发生了这么大的剧情转折，

926
00:42:37.240 --> 00:42:40.600
but I couldn't get my eyes off a heater under John's desk.
但我实在无法把目光从约翰桌下的取暖器上移开。

927
00:42:40.680 --> 00:42:41.080
Wow.
哇。

928
00:42:41.660 --> 00:42:42.480
Check it out.
快看。

929
00:42:43.620 --> 00:42:44.600
And it's on.
而且它是开着的。

930
00:42:44.860 --> 00:42:45.040
Yeah.
是的。

931
00:42:45.200 --> 00:42:47.000
The little red light is on.
那个小红灯亮着呢。

932
00:42:48.020 --> 00:42:50.860
Well, Toby's going to come in to see what's going on.
好吧，托比会进来看看发生了什么事。

933
00:42:51.280 --> 00:42:54.040
Kelly's going to say that Dwight went on a shooting spree.
凯莉会说德怀特刚才疯狂扫射。

934
00:42:54.600 --> 00:42:57.200
Background catch at 11 minutes, 45 seconds.
背景细节捕捉，11分45秒。

935
00:42:57.660 --> 00:43:00.760
Did you guys catch that Dwight hands his gun to Creed?
你们注意到德怀特把枪递给克里德了吗？

936
00:43:01.080 --> 00:43:02.860
And I guess Creed is going to get rid of it?
我猜克里德是要去处理掉它？

937
00:43:03.520 --> 00:43:03.960
Yeah.
是的。

938
00:43:04.220 --> 00:43:07.940
I mean, if anyone knows how to get rid of a gun in this office, it's probably Creed.
我的意思是，如果办公室里有人知道怎么处理掉一把枪，那大概就是克里德了。

939
00:43:08.160 --> 00:43:09.160
Just such a great...
真是太棒了……

940
00:43:09.160 --> 00:43:11.680
Don't you think maybe this isn't the first gun he's gotten rid of?
你不觉得这可能不是他处理掉的第一把枪吗？

941
00:43:11.760 --> 00:43:12.600
I'm just saying.
我只是随口一说。

942
00:43:12.860 --> 00:43:14.160
I mean, he lives under the desk.
我是说，他住在桌子底下。

943
00:43:14.160 --> 00:43:15.640
He has a whole other life in Canada.
他在加拿大还有另一段完整的人生。

944
00:43:15.940 --> 00:43:16.600
We don't know.
我们不知道。

945
00:43:16.720 --> 00:43:17.240
We don't know.
我们不知道。

946
00:43:17.940 --> 00:43:23.400
Well, Oscar wants to look up some of Andy's symptoms on WebMD, which gets some great
好吧，奥斯卡想在WebMD上查查安迪的症状，这引来了安吉拉的

947
00:43:23.400 --> 00:43:24.500
snark from Angela.
冷嘲热讽。

948
00:43:24.500 --> 00:43:28.460
This is one of my favorite Angela Martin lines of all of season seven.
这是我最喜欢的安吉拉·马丁在第七季中的台词之一。

949
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:33.440
In the script, it was written like this, and we shot it exactly as it was written.
剧本里就是这么写的，我们拍摄时也完全照着剧本演的。

950
00:43:34.060 --> 00:43:35.800
Oscar says, I'll look on WebMD.
奥斯卡说，我会在WebMD上查查。

951
00:43:35.920 --> 00:43:36.700
What are your symptoms?
你有什么症状？

952
00:43:37.440 --> 00:43:40.020
Angela, in parentheses, sarcastic.
安吉拉，括号里写着，讽刺地。

953
00:43:40.780 --> 00:43:44.200
Oh, everybody, Oscar found a reason to look on WebMD.
噢，大家快看，奥斯卡又在网上查病了。

954
00:43:44.560 --> 00:43:47.040
I love the assumed history of these two characters.
我喜欢这两个角色之间那种默认的过往。

955
00:43:47.280 --> 00:43:52.640
I love knowing that he looks on WebMD so much that it has driven her crazy for years.
我喜欢这种设定，他查网页查得太多，以至于多年来一直让她抓狂。

956
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:59.300
I think it's lines like this that really made this feel like a nostalgic old office episode.
我觉得正是这样的台词，让这一集真的很有那种怀旧老版《办公室》的感觉。

957
00:43:59.560 --> 00:44:01.740
And also like the stuff at the copier.
还有复印机那边的戏份也是。

958
00:44:01.880 --> 00:44:06.920
We just brought back, I feel like, some of that mundane office work kind of stuff.
我觉得我们只是带回了一些那种平淡的办公室日常琐事。

959
00:44:07.040 --> 00:44:07.220
Yeah.
没错。

960
00:44:07.460 --> 00:44:08.820
And relationship stuff.
还有人际关系方面的事。

961
00:44:09.200 --> 00:44:09.580
Yeah.
没错。

962
00:44:09.580 --> 00:44:19.500
I want you to know that when Toby gets excited to go get his new safety binder, I really felt that I would be excited to use a new binder.
我想让你知道，当托比兴奋地去拿他的新安全手册时，我真的感同身受，因为我也很乐意用一本新活页夹。

963
00:44:19.780 --> 00:44:24.000
You know, I have a lot of stuff in my house that is for various emergencies.
你知道，我家里有很多应对各种紧急情况的东西。

964
00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:31.040
And I'm not saying that I want a zombie apocalypse or that I want any kind of apocalypse or end of times.
我不是说我想要僵尸末日，或者任何形式的末日或世界末日。

965
00:44:31.320 --> 00:44:37.940
But if it happened, I would be so excited to grab my expired medications book bag.
但如果真的发生了，我会非常兴奋地抓起我的过期药品急救包。

966
00:44:38.660 --> 00:44:41.640
You know, I would just be like, I knew it!
你知道，我会觉得，我就知道会有这一天！

967
00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:45.440
I really can't wait for you to meet the character of Bill in The Last of Us.
我真的迫不及待想让你看看《最后生还者》里的比尔这个角色。

968
00:44:45.540 --> 00:44:47.040
I need you to meet Bill.
你一定要认识一下比尔。

969
00:44:47.220 --> 00:44:47.480
Okay.
好的。

970
00:44:47.480 --> 00:44:49.000
I'm not going to say anything else.
我什么都不会再说了。

971
00:44:49.200 --> 00:44:49.380
All right.
好吧。

972
00:44:49.740 --> 00:44:54.840
But speaking of Toby and how excited he was, you know, to have his emergency binder.
但说到托比，他当时为了拿到紧急手册有多兴奋，你知道的。

973
00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:59.760
Jenna, do you remember when we were filming this when Paul came out to say all that?
珍娜，你还记得我们拍这一段时，保罗出来说那些话的情景吗？

974
00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:01.060
He had to address the bullpen.
他必须向办公区的人发表讲话。

975
00:45:01.220 --> 00:45:01.440
Yes.
记得。

976
00:45:01.640 --> 00:45:04.200
And he mumbled so badly we couldn't understand him.
他嘟囔得太厉害了，我们根本听不清他在说什么。

977
00:45:04.620 --> 00:45:06.020
We even improvised.
我们甚至还即兴发挥了。

978
00:45:06.180 --> 00:45:07.660
What are you saying, Toby?
你在说什么，托比？

979
00:45:08.040 --> 00:45:08.920
Speak up!
大声点！

980
00:45:09.580 --> 00:45:11.240
We started laughing so hard.
我们当时笑得太厉害了。

981
00:45:11.240 --> 00:45:16.960
And I don't know if it was Paul or Paul being Toby, but he really struggled getting that line out.
我不知道那是保罗本人还是保罗在演托比，但他确实很难把那句台词说出来。

982
00:45:16.960 --> 00:45:18.980
I feel like that made it onto the bloopers.
我觉得那段进了花絮里。

983
00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:26.300
It definitely made it on, you know, they would do blooper reels and stuff for our end of season cast parties that we would have.
它绝对进去了，你知道的，我们每季结束时的剧组派对上都会放花絮集锦之类的东西。

984
00:45:26.440 --> 00:45:28.420
And I remember it was definitely on there.
我记得那段肯定在里面。

985
00:45:29.500 --> 00:45:37.540
Dwight is now going to do his best Michael, which is where he calls a conference room meeting and creates a character to cover up his screw up.
德怀特现在要尽力模仿迈克尔了，也就是他召集会议室开会，并创造一个角色来掩盖自己的失误。

986
00:45:37.660 --> 00:45:39.160
Gun safety Dwight!
枪支安全员德怀特！

987
00:45:39.520 --> 00:45:39.860
Yeah.
没错。

988
00:45:40.120 --> 00:45:41.660
I'm the rootinist toot.
我是最厉害的枪手。

989
00:45:41.720 --> 00:45:42.740
And he just can't do it.
但他根本做不到。

990
00:45:42.840 --> 00:45:43.760
He fails immediately.
他立刻就失败了。

991
00:45:44.080 --> 00:45:44.460
He does.
确实。

992
00:45:44.660 --> 00:45:46.580
He does give a pretty great speech, though.
不过他确实发表了一段很棒的演讲。

993
00:45:46.580 --> 00:45:47.180
He says,
他说，

994
00:45:47.500 --> 00:45:50.820
Managing you for this last week has been the greatest honor of my life.
过去这一周管理你们是我一生中最大的荣幸。

995
00:45:50.960 --> 00:45:53.980
And if you ruin this, I will burn this office to the ground.
如果你们搞砸了，我会把这间办公室烧成平地。

996
00:45:54.140 --> 00:45:59.200
And I mean that figuratively, not literally, because you guys are so, so important to me.
我是比喻，不是字面意思，因为你们对我来说非常非常重要。

997
00:45:59.480 --> 00:46:00.620
I love you guys.
我爱你们。

998
00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:01.860
But don't cross me.
但别惹我。

999
00:46:02.140 --> 00:46:03.120
But you're the beSt.
你们是最棒的。

1000
00:46:03.620 --> 00:46:07.420
Rain said that that final monologue at the end was really hard for him to get through.
雷恩说最后那段独白对他来说真的很难演完。

1001
00:46:07.840 --> 00:46:13.860
And it was really in that moment that he realized everything Steve went through leading those conference room meetings.
就在那一刻，他真正体会到了史蒂夫主持那些会议室会议时所经历的一切。

1002
00:46:13.860 --> 00:46:14.240
Yeah.
没错。

1003
00:46:15.060 --> 00:46:19.840
I thought he did such a great job, though, because he had to turn on a dime back and forth, back and forth.
不过我觉得他做得非常出色，因为他必须在两种状态之间来回切换，反复横跳。

1004
00:46:19.880 --> 00:46:20.240
Many times.
很多次。

1005
00:46:20.500 --> 00:46:20.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1006
00:46:21.420 --> 00:46:23.560
Andy and Daryl are going to come back from the hospital.
安迪和达里尔要从医院回来了。

1007
00:46:24.240 --> 00:46:26.180
Andy's got like a little bandage on his ear.
安迪的耳朵上贴着个小绷带。

1008
00:46:26.180 --> 00:46:30.240
And he shares with everyone that he ruptured his eardrum.
他告诉大家他的耳膜穿孔了。

1009
00:46:30.480 --> 00:46:31.140
That's right.
没错。

1010
00:46:31.360 --> 00:46:33.860
And he has temporary deafness in that ear.
而且那只耳朵暂时失聪了。

1011
00:46:34.040 --> 00:46:34.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1012
00:46:35.440 --> 00:46:38.720
I have a deep dive on burst eardruMs.
我对耳膜穿孔做了一番深入研究。

1013
00:46:40.200 --> 00:46:45.720
Wait, before you go on this deep dive, I have to tell you one thing.
等等，在你开始深入讲解之前，我得告诉你一件事。

1014
00:46:46.380 --> 00:46:52.220
Justin said on the commentary, he said they were so worried that people were going to get grossed out by this injury.
贾斯汀在评论音轨里说，他们当时非常担心观众会被这个伤口恶心到。

1015
00:46:52.380 --> 00:46:52.760
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1016
00:46:53.220 --> 00:46:55.840
That they were trying to find different ways to word it.
所以他们一直在想各种不同的表达方式。

1017
00:46:56.000 --> 00:46:59.980
And at one point in the script, they had Andy saying, my ear don't work so good.
剧本里有一版台词是让安迪说：我的耳朵不太好使了。

1018
00:47:00.660 --> 00:47:01.100
Oh.
哦。

1019
00:47:01.100 --> 00:47:02.500
My ear no-do work.
我的耳朵不工作了。

1020
00:47:02.620 --> 00:47:04.300
They had all these different phrases.
他们想了各种各样的说法。

1021
00:47:05.160 --> 00:47:09.400
But ultimately, they had to say, you know, that he's going to have this injured eardrum.
但最终，他们还是不得不说，你知道的，他耳膜受伤了。

1022
00:47:09.760 --> 00:47:13.980
And I just feel like I have to bring that up because I don't know what to expect from this deep dive.
我之所以一定要提这个，是因为我不知道你接下来的深入讲解会讲出什么来。

1023
00:47:14.140 --> 00:47:19.120
If they were worried, a group of writers who had researched it, that people were going to get grossed out.
如果连那群做过调研的编剧都担心观众会感到恶心的话。

1024
00:47:19.940 --> 00:47:24.080
I'm not going to explain everything that happens when you have a burst eardrum.
我不会解释耳膜穿孔后发生的所有细节。

1025
00:47:24.200 --> 00:47:24.620
Thank you.
谢谢。

1026
00:47:24.920 --> 00:47:30.880
Except to say that the symptoms that Andy complains about are symptoms of a burst eardrum.
我只想说，安迪抱怨的那些症状确实是耳膜穿孔的症状。

1027
00:47:31.100 --> 00:47:35.560
The ringing in the ear, the hearing loss, the pain, all of those things.
耳鸣、听力丧失、疼痛，所有这些。

1028
00:47:36.140 --> 00:47:41.920
What I got curious about was, can a loud noise burst your eardrum?
我感到好奇的是，巨大的噪音真的能震破耳膜吗？

1029
00:47:42.040 --> 00:47:43.040
Is that true?
这是真的吗？

1030
00:47:43.360 --> 00:47:47.300
Is that possible that this gunshot sound burst his eardrum?
那种枪声真的有可能震破他的耳膜吗？

1031
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:48.020
Sure.
当然。

1032
00:47:48.020 --> 00:47:49.260
I'm going to say sure.
我会说当然可以。

1033
00:47:49.640 --> 00:47:50.800
The answer is yes.
答案是肯定的。

1034
00:47:50.800 --> 00:48:06.000
You can get a perforated eardrum, which is a burst eardrum, from a loud sound, a foreign object in your ear, like a Q-tip, head trauma, an ear infection, or rapid pressure changes.
耳膜穿孔，也就是耳膜破裂，可能是由巨大的声响、耳内的异物（比如棉签）、头部外伤、耳部感染或气压剧烈变化引起的。

1035
00:48:06.840 --> 00:48:08.480
Like on a plane.
比如在飞机上。

1036
00:48:08.480 --> 00:48:12.620
Or going down into the ocean, you know, if you dive down too faSt.
或者潜入深海，你知道的，如果你下潜得太快。

1037
00:48:12.840 --> 00:48:13.060
Yeah.
没错。

1038
00:48:13.480 --> 00:48:14.640
Or a submarine, sure.
或者潜水艇，当然。

1039
00:48:15.260 --> 00:48:18.420
Just going to yell different modes of transportation.
我只是在列举各种交通工具。

1040
00:48:18.760 --> 00:48:18.880
Sure.
当然。

1041
00:48:19.080 --> 00:48:20.700
To either up high or down low.
无论是去高处还是去深处。

1042
00:48:21.340 --> 00:48:29.020
But getting back to this idea of your eardrum rupturing from a loud noise, I wanted to know, like, how loud does the noise have to be?
回到耳膜因巨大噪音而破裂这个话题，我想知道，噪音到底要多大才行？

1043
00:48:29.020 --> 00:48:37.200
And, according to Better Hearing of Austin, it would have to be 165 decibels or more.
根据奥斯汀听力改善中心的说法，噪音需要达到165分贝或以上。

1044
00:48:37.660 --> 00:48:46.120
And that would be consistent with a gunshot at close range, fireworks, or extremely loud music.
这与近距离枪声、烟花或极高分贝的音乐是一致的。

1045
00:48:46.360 --> 00:48:49.160
So, I mean, I had to keep going here.
所以，我的意思是，我得继续查下去。

1046
00:48:49.380 --> 00:48:51.460
How loud of the music.
音乐得有多大声才行。

1047
00:48:51.640 --> 00:48:52.100
Okay.
好吧。

1048
00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:55.240
You know, my son plays in a rock band.
你知道，我儿子在一个摇滚乐队里演奏。

1049
00:48:55.420 --> 00:48:55.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1050
00:48:55.880 --> 00:48:58.860
He wears headphones, but I'm like, what?
他戴着耳机，但我心想，什么？

1051
00:48:59.020 --> 00:48:59.800
You know?
你知道吗？

1052
00:49:00.540 --> 00:49:05.660
So, the average decibel level of a rock concert is 100 decibels.
摇滚演唱会的平均分贝水平是100分贝。

1053
00:49:05.660 --> 00:49:06.860
So, well below.
所以，远低于这个数值。

1054
00:49:07.180 --> 00:49:07.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1055
00:49:08.100 --> 00:49:15.460
However, there have been several rock concerts that have registered levels of up to 130 decibels.
然而，曾有几场摇滚演唱会记录到的分贝水平高达130分贝。

1056
00:49:15.660 --> 00:49:16.880
Do you know who they were?
你知道是哪些乐队吗？

1057
00:49:17.180 --> 00:49:17.660
Oh.
噢。

1058
00:49:17.660 --> 00:49:21.260
These are the loudest rock bands on record.
这些是有记录以来声音最大的摇滚乐队。

1059
00:49:21.660 --> 00:49:22.940
There's four of them.
一共有四支。

1060
00:49:23.180 --> 00:49:23.780
Metallica?
金属乐队（Metallica）？

1061
00:49:24.120 --> 00:49:24.800
No.
不是。

1062
00:49:25.260 --> 00:49:25.440
Oh.
噢。

1063
00:49:26.000 --> 00:49:26.820
Good guess.
猜得不错。

1064
00:49:28.340 --> 00:49:29.420
Here they are.
就是这些。

1065
00:49:29.740 --> 00:49:30.760
Led Zeppelin.
齐柏林飞艇（Led Zeppelin）。

1066
00:49:30.960 --> 00:49:31.200
Oh.
噢。

1067
00:49:31.860 --> 00:49:32.460
ACDC.
AC/DC乐队。

1068
00:49:32.580 --> 00:49:33.580
I was going to say ACDC.
我本来想说AC/DC的。

1069
00:49:34.120 --> 00:49:34.420
Yep.
没错。

1070
00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:35.600
Motorhead.
摩托头乐队（Motorhead）。

1071
00:49:36.260 --> 00:49:36.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1072
00:49:37.120 --> 00:49:37.980
And Ted Nugent.
还有泰德·纽金特（Ted Nugent）。

1073
00:49:38.580 --> 00:49:40.420
They're all very loud.
他们都非常吵。

1074
00:49:40.420 --> 00:49:42.040
I was about to say ACDC.
我刚才正要说AC/DC。

1075
00:49:42.260 --> 00:49:42.980
I really was.
我真的要说了。

1076
00:49:43.140 --> 00:49:45.040
I was going to say ACDC or Metallica.
我本来打算说AC/DC或者金属乐队的。

1077
00:49:45.140 --> 00:49:46.920
So, I kind of got one on the liSt.
所以，榜单上我算猜中了一个。

1078
00:49:47.760 --> 00:49:52.000
Sporting events have also recorded very high decibel levels.
体育赛事也记录过非常高的分贝水平。

1079
00:49:52.120 --> 00:49:56.260
And the loudest one on record belongs to a certain football team.
而有记录以来最吵的一次属于某支橄榄球队。

1080
00:49:56.260 --> 00:49:57.380
It was a home game.
那是一场主场比赛。

1081
00:49:57.640 --> 00:50:01.520
It came in at 142.2 decibels.
达到了142.2分贝。

1082
00:50:01.520 --> 00:50:06.940
Okay, this would have to be a team that plays in some kind of a dome, right, to contain the sound.
好吧，这支球队一定是在某种圆顶体育场里比赛，对吧，这样才能聚拢声音。

1083
00:50:07.160 --> 00:50:08.740
I don't know anything about where they play.
我不知道他们在哪儿比赛。

1084
00:50:08.920 --> 00:50:10.500
I bet it's a team with a dome.
我敢打赌那是一支有圆顶体育场的球队。

1085
00:50:10.820 --> 00:50:11.880
That's what I'm going to say.
我打算就这么猜。

1086
00:50:12.020 --> 00:50:14.120
They're very topical right now.
他们最近正热门呢。

1087
00:50:15.020 --> 00:50:16.380
The Philadelphia Eagles?
费城老鹰队（Philadelphia Eagles）？

1088
00:50:16.800 --> 00:50:17.200
Nope.
不是。

1089
00:50:17.360 --> 00:50:19.100
The Kansas City Chiefs.
堪萨斯城酋长队（Kansas City Chiefs）。

1090
00:50:19.100 --> 00:50:20.520
So, I knew it would be one of them.
我就知道会是他们其中之一。

1091
00:50:20.780 --> 00:50:21.700
Loudest one.
最吵的那一个。

1092
00:50:21.860 --> 00:50:24.580
They took the record away from the Seahawks.
他们从海鹰队（Seahawks）手中夺走了这个纪录。

1093
00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:38.120
I want you to know that just for some perspective, 142.2 decibels is louder than if you were standing under a jet airplane flying 100 feet above your head.
我想让你知道，为了让你有个概念，142.2分贝比你站在一架从头顶上方100英尺处飞过的喷气式飞机下还要吵。

1094
00:50:38.260 --> 00:50:38.660
Wow.
哇。

1095
00:50:38.940 --> 00:50:41.080
That's how loud that was in the stadium.
体育场里的声音就是那么大。

1096
00:50:41.480 --> 00:50:42.960
I'm looking up their stadium.
我正在查他们的体育场。

1097
00:50:43.360 --> 00:50:44.940
You want to know if it's a dome?
你想知道是不是圆顶的？

1098
00:50:45.320 --> 00:50:45.620
Yeah.
是的。

1099
00:50:46.240 --> 00:50:48.580
Well, those Chiefs fans are loud.
嗯，那些酋长队的球迷确实很吵。

1100
00:50:49.500 --> 00:50:50.720
It's not a dome.
那不是圆顶体育场。

1101
00:50:50.960 --> 00:50:51.320
It's not.
并不是。

1102
00:50:51.420 --> 00:50:52.540
That's how loud they are.
它们的声音就是那么大。

1103
00:50:52.920 --> 00:50:53.680
Open air.
露天的。

1104
00:50:54.360 --> 00:50:54.760
Wow.
哇。

1105
00:50:55.200 --> 00:50:55.460
Yep.
没错。

1106
00:50:55.960 --> 00:50:57.940
I did say hi to Patrick Mahomes once.
我确实跟帕特里克·马霍姆斯打过一次招呼。

1107
00:50:58.580 --> 00:50:59.200
You did?
真的吗？

1108
00:50:59.420 --> 00:50:59.680
I did.
真的。

1109
00:50:59.780 --> 00:51:00.700
I just said, hi, Patrick.
我就说了句，嗨，帕特里克。

1110
00:51:00.860 --> 00:51:01.480
He said, what's up?
他说，怎么了？

1111
00:51:01.700 --> 00:51:03.920
What are the circumstances of you meeting him?
你们是在什么情况下见面的？

1112
00:51:04.080 --> 00:51:09.940
I was on the field at a Broncos game, and he was warming up, and I walked past him, and I was like, oh, that's Patrick Mahomes.
当时我在野马队比赛的球场上，他正在热身，我从他身边走过，心想，哦，那是帕特里克·马霍姆斯。

1113
00:51:10.060 --> 00:51:10.800
So, I said, hi, Patrick.
于是我就说，嗨，帕特里克。

1114
00:51:11.340 --> 00:51:12.280
He said, what's up?
他说，怎么了？

1115
00:51:12.600 --> 00:51:14.560
Oh, what a pleasant exchange.
哦，真是愉快的交流。

1116
00:51:14.880 --> 00:51:18.820
I think I slightly embarrassed my kids because I think I just was so casual.
我觉得我稍微有点让我的孩子们尴尬，因为我觉得我当时表现得太随意了。

1117
00:51:19.100 --> 00:51:19.560
Hi, Patrick.
嗨，帕特里克。

1118
00:51:20.420 --> 00:51:21.540
Like, I was his neighbor.
就像我是他邻居一样。

1119
00:51:22.220 --> 00:51:23.500
But he was very nice.
但他非常友善。

1120
00:51:23.640 --> 00:51:24.220
He was nice.
他很友善。

1121
00:51:24.420 --> 00:51:28.040
You know who I just ran into on a hike who was like a total blowhard?
你知道我刚才在徒步时遇到了谁吗？那人简直是个自大狂。

1122
00:51:28.700 --> 00:51:30.500
Oh, you're going to tell this story?
哦，你要讲这个故事吗？

1123
00:51:31.040 --> 00:51:39.960
I ran into a very famous musician who was walking his two dogs on the same hike that I was walking on, and he mansplained me about dogs.
我在徒步时遇到了一位非常有名的音乐家，他正带着他的两条狗在同一条路上走，他居然跟我大谈特谈养狗经。

1124
00:51:40.260 --> 00:51:44.780
And then I said something to Lee about it, and Lee said, oh, yeah, he's a famous mansplainer.
后来我跟李说了这件事，李说，哦，对，他是个有名的说教男。

1125
00:51:45.320 --> 00:51:48.680
Who was the famous musician mansplainer?
那个爱说教的著名音乐家是谁？

1126
00:51:48.820 --> 00:51:49.520
I don't know.
我不知道。

1127
00:51:50.140 --> 00:51:51.300
I'll tell you after.
我待会儿告诉你。

1128
00:51:51.660 --> 00:51:52.900
Give me one hint.
给我一个提示。

1129
00:51:56.300 --> 00:51:57.460
I don't know how to give you a hint.
我不知道该怎么给你提示。

1130
00:51:57.460 --> 00:51:57.640
Breather.
喘气的人。

1131
00:51:57.800 --> 00:51:58.460
Heavy breather.
重度喘气者。

1132
00:51:58.820 --> 00:52:00.120
No, he's very tall.
不，他个子很高。

1133
00:52:00.280 --> 00:52:01.180
That was just you signing.
那只是你在叹气。

1134
00:52:01.180 --> 00:52:01.760
How about that?
那怎么样？

1135
00:52:01.760 --> 00:52:02.600
He's very tall.
他个子非常高。

1136
00:52:02.840 --> 00:52:04.320
Oh, everybody's tall to me.
哦，对我来说每个人个子都高。

1137
00:52:04.860 --> 00:52:09.180
Well, guys, we've got another episode of Office Ladies Burn It to the Ground.
好了，伙计们，我们又迎来了一期《办公室女士：彻底摧毁》。

1138
00:52:09.720 --> 00:52:12.740
He clearly pissed you off on this hike.
他在这次徒步中显然惹火了你。

1139
00:52:13.460 --> 00:52:16.160
Because I didn't say anything to this person.
因为我根本没跟这个人说话。

1140
00:52:16.320 --> 00:52:17.880
He just started talking to you.
他只是开始跟你搭话。

1141
00:52:18.060 --> 00:52:19.280
He just started in.
他直接就开始了。

1142
00:52:19.460 --> 00:52:20.660
I'm just tall.
我只是个子高。

1143
00:52:20.860 --> 00:52:24.300
And I'm just going to mansplain to you about dogs.
我就要给你科普一下养狗知识。

1144
00:52:24.900 --> 00:52:27.020
I didn't ask for advice.
我没寻求建议。

1145
00:52:27.420 --> 00:52:29.760
I didn't even say, what kind of dog do you have?
我甚至都没问，你养的是什么狗？

1146
00:52:29.820 --> 00:52:33.400
I gave no indication that I even wanted to be spoken to.
我完全没表现出我想被搭话的意思。

1147
00:52:33.880 --> 00:52:39.160
I'm sure you gave off the body language I know that you have sometimes, which is don't talk to me.
我相信你当时肯定散发出那种你有时会有的肢体语言，就是“别跟我说话”。

1148
00:52:39.180 --> 00:52:40.500
That I have sometimes.
我有时确实会有。

1149
00:52:40.760 --> 00:52:41.900
That's my default.
那是我的默认状态。

1150
00:52:42.760 --> 00:52:45.020
I almost never want to be talked to.
我几乎从来不想被搭话。

1151
00:52:45.140 --> 00:52:46.020
I am an introvert.
我是个内向的人。

1152
00:52:46.160 --> 00:52:47.140
I was trying to be nice.
我当时只是想表现得友善点。

1153
00:52:47.200 --> 00:52:49.120
I just want to walk my dog on a hike.
我只想带我的狗去徒步。

1154
00:52:49.280 --> 00:52:50.280
And be left alone.
然后别来打扰我。

1155
00:52:50.400 --> 00:52:50.780
Exactly.
没错。

1156
00:52:51.260 --> 00:52:52.140
Leave me alone, tall people.
别来烦我，高个子们。

1157
00:52:52.340 --> 00:52:53.740
What's so hard about that?
这有什么难的吗？

1158
00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:56.500
My dog had to stop and get a drink of water.
我的狗得停下来喝口水。

1159
00:52:56.660 --> 00:53:00.400
That was not an invitation to talk to me.
那可不是邀请你来跟我搭话。

1160
00:53:00.520 --> 00:53:00.580
Man's plane.
男人的飞机。

1161
00:53:00.800 --> 00:53:01.500
It wasn't.
并不是。

1162
00:53:02.420 --> 00:53:03.560
Back to the episode.
回到剧集内容。

1163
00:53:04.420 --> 00:53:08.300
People are catching on now that Dwight doesn't want Joe to know about this.
大家现在都看出来了，德怀特不想让乔知道这件事。

1164
00:53:08.300 --> 00:53:09.960
And they start making demands of him.
于是他们开始向他提要求。

1165
00:53:10.860 --> 00:53:11.140
Yes.
是的。

1166
00:53:11.800 --> 00:53:14.960
Kelly asked for a day off to audition for American Idol.
凯莉请了一天假去参加《美国偶像》的海选。

1167
00:53:15.180 --> 00:53:15.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1168
00:53:15.980 --> 00:53:17.820
Phyllis wants an extra vacation day.
菲利斯想要多一天假期。

1169
00:53:18.240 --> 00:53:20.040
Angela wants pet day back.
安吉拉想要恢复宠物日。

1170
00:53:20.200 --> 00:53:20.920
No dogs.
不准带狗。

1171
00:53:21.440 --> 00:53:23.600
Kevin wants everything back in the vending machine.
凯文想要自动贩卖机恢复原样。

1172
00:53:23.780 --> 00:53:25.000
Except the fruit.
除了水果。

1173
00:53:25.840 --> 00:53:30.180
Pam wants Dwight to get rid of all of his weapons, including the killer fish.
帕姆想要德怀特处理掉他所有的武器，包括那条杀人鱼。

1174
00:53:30.180 --> 00:53:36.800
Jim wants Dwight to work in the phrase, shagadelic baby, into conversation with Joe and do jazz
吉姆想要德怀特在和乔谈话时加入“摇摆宝贝”这个短语，并且在吉姆咳嗽时做爵士

1175
00:53:36.800 --> 00:53:38.880
hands anytime Jim coughs.
手势。

1176
00:53:39.240 --> 00:53:40.400
But there was more.
但还有更多。

1177
00:53:40.680 --> 00:53:43.060
There were more demands that we didn't see?
还有我们没看到的更多要求？

1178
00:53:43.340 --> 00:53:43.820
Yes.
是的。

1179
00:53:43.820 --> 00:53:46.320
Yes, that we filmed because they were in the shooting draft.
是的，我们拍了，因为它们在拍摄剧本里。

1180
00:53:46.880 --> 00:53:50.200
First of all, Dwight is going to offer to pay for Andy's medical bills.
首先，德怀特提出要支付安迪的医疗费。

1181
00:53:50.580 --> 00:53:51.040
Okay.
好吧。

1182
00:53:51.320 --> 00:53:51.660
Fair.
公平。

1183
00:53:51.920 --> 00:53:52.420
Fair.
公平。

1184
00:53:52.660 --> 00:53:52.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1185
00:53:52.960 --> 00:53:54.960
And then Andy says, but you know what?
然后安迪说，但你知道吗？

1186
00:53:54.960 --> 00:53:58.440
I also can't go to my swimming class at the Y and I already paid for those.
我也没法去基督教青年会的游泳课了，而且我已经付过钱了。

1187
00:53:59.220 --> 00:54:01.640
So Dwight's going to have to pay for his swimming classes.
所以德怀特得支付他的游泳课费用。

1188
00:54:01.680 --> 00:54:01.800
Swimming classes.
游泳课。

1189
00:54:02.980 --> 00:54:06.440
Daryl wants Dwight to honor the night school that D'Angelo had promised him.
达里尔想要德怀特兑现迪安杰洛承诺给他的夜校课程。

1190
00:54:06.600 --> 00:54:07.280
Also fair.
这也算公平。

1191
00:54:07.980 --> 00:54:11.540
Aaron wants a new nameplate that doesn't say receptioniSt.
亚伦想要一个新的名牌，上面不要写着“接待员”。

1192
00:54:12.100 --> 00:54:12.560
Oh.
哦。

1193
00:54:12.900 --> 00:54:13.520
I know.
我知道。

1194
00:54:14.160 --> 00:54:16.100
Stanley has the best one of the bunch.
斯坦利的要求是这堆里最棒的。

1195
00:54:16.500 --> 00:54:17.140
Ready for this?
准备好听这个了吗？

1196
00:54:17.140 --> 00:54:22.580
He says, I want to start telecommuting from home because I am concerned for my safety in
他说，我想开始居家办公，因为我担心我在

1197
00:54:22.580 --> 00:54:23.200
this office.
这个办公室的安全。

1198
00:54:24.120 --> 00:54:24.860
Dwight agrees.
德怀特同意了。

1199
00:54:25.460 --> 00:54:26.760
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1200
00:54:27.220 --> 00:54:31.180
And lastly, Creed wants Dwight's eyes.
最后，克里德想要德怀特的眼睛。

1201
00:54:32.420 --> 00:54:33.320
Not now.
现在不行。

1202
00:54:33.480 --> 00:54:34.440
Once he is dead.
等他死了以后。

1203
00:54:34.560 --> 00:54:35.620
He lets him know that.
他会让他知道这一点。

1204
00:54:35.900 --> 00:54:36.160
Okay.
好吧。

1205
00:54:36.720 --> 00:54:37.480
There you go.
这就对了。

1206
00:54:37.640 --> 00:54:38.940
Those were everyone's demands.
这就是所有人的要求。

1207
00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:42.860
Well, in the next scene, Dwight's going to be exiting the men's bathroom.
嗯，在下一场戏里，德怀特要从男厕所出来。

1208
00:54:42.860 --> 00:54:44.780
He's holding an empty fish tank.
他手里拿着一个空鱼缸。

1209
00:54:44.780 --> 00:54:49.220
It's very clear that he has, I guess, flushed his piranha down the toilet.
很明显，我猜他是把食人鱼冲进马桶里了。

1210
00:54:49.700 --> 00:54:50.880
Kevin enters.
凯文进来了。

1211
00:54:51.500 --> 00:54:54.120
Fan question from Madison B in Melbourne, Australia.
来自澳大利亚墨尔本的麦迪逊·B的粉丝提问。

1212
00:54:55.020 --> 00:55:00.060
The short scene in which Dwight dumps his piranha into the toilet leading to Kevin discovering
德怀特把食人鱼倒进马桶，导致凯文发现它们的那场短戏，

1213
00:55:00.060 --> 00:55:03.500
them has to be one of my favorite moments in the whole show.
绝对是我整部剧中最喜欢的时刻之一。

1214
00:55:03.680 --> 00:55:07.720
It causes me to cry from laughter every time I rewatch it.
每次重看我都会笑出眼泪。

1215
00:55:08.120 --> 00:55:11.260
Kevin moves so fast out of there and is so shocked.
凯文跑得那么快，而且那么震惊。

1216
00:55:11.880 --> 00:55:14.580
Madison, I loved Brian Bomber's performance.
麦迪逊，我很喜欢布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳的表演。

1217
00:55:14.780 --> 00:55:15.860
In this short moment.
就在这短短的一瞬间。

1218
00:55:16.100 --> 00:55:17.120
It is perfection.
简直完美。

1219
00:55:17.700 --> 00:55:18.940
It's so believable.
太真实了。

1220
00:55:19.300 --> 00:55:26.400
Like, I fully believe that Kevin just completely lost it because he was about to sit on a fish.
我完全相信凯文当时彻底崩溃了，因为他差点就坐到一条鱼身上。

1221
00:55:26.920 --> 00:55:31.760
I am assuming everyone out there knows how standards and practices felt about Kevin's F-bomb.
我想大家应该都知道审查部门对凯文那句脏话的看法。

1222
00:55:32.300 --> 00:55:36.480
We got the usual bleep full word, blur lip flap, or stage off camera.
我们通常会用消音处理完整单词，模糊嘴部动作，或者让演员在镜头外说。

1223
00:55:36.680 --> 00:55:38.620
Stage off camera is always my favorite note.
“在镜头外说”总是我最喜欢的修改意见。

1224
